package ${package};

/**
 * One contract case: a request, and the response the contract declares for it. Derived from
 * the contract alone, and listed, in canonical order, by {@code CASES} on each operation's
 * {@code ContractCases} class: success cases, then not found, not acceptable, unsupported media
 * type, and the invalid requests.
 *
 * <p>Each request is one the contract accepts, or differs from one in exactly one place. Its
 * values are raw: encoding them for the path, the query or a header is the renderer's job.
 * Every case but a not-acceptable one sends the same {@code Accept}: every media type the
 * operation's responses declare.
 *
 * <p>What a target's fixture must do before a case's request is sent:
 *
 * <table>
 *   <caption>The fixture, per kind</caption>
 *   <tr><th>Kind</th><th>Real implementation</th><th>Double</th></tr>
 *   <tr><td>{@code SUCCESS}</td><td>Put the service in the state that makes this status the right
 *   answer: the resource exists for a read, an update or a delete, and does not exist for a
 *   create.</td><td>Serve the case's response.</td></tr>
 *   <tr><td>{@code NOT_FOUND}</td><td>Make sure the resource the path names does not
 *   exist.</td><td>Serve the case's response.</td></tr>
 *   <tr><td>Every other kind</td><td>Nothing: the request is refused before any state is
 *   consulted.</td><td>Serve the case's response.</td></tr>
 * </table>
 *
 * <p>A case that does not require state is refused by a correct implementation without anything
 * being stored, but one the implementation wrongly accepts may leave state behind for the cases
 * after it: such a test is only as independent as the implementation is correct. A case that
 * requires state is the opposite: with a correct fixture it is independent and repeatable.
 *
 * @param id                   readable, unique within its operation and the same on every run,
 *                             such as {@code success-201-required} or
 *                             {@code body-emailAddress-maxLength}; a test method name and a
 *                             snippet directory can be made from it
 * @param kind                 what the case tests
 * @param requiresState        whether the target must be put in a particular state before the
 *                             request is sent: true for {@code SUCCESS} and {@code NOT_FOUND}
 * @param variant              for a success case, the valid request it sends: {@code required},
 *                             {@code full} or {@code noBody}; null for every other kind
 * @param description          one sentence saying what the request is
 * @param in                   for an invalid request, where the fault is: {@code path},
 *                             {@code query}, {@code header} or {@code body}; null otherwise
 * @param name                 for an invalid request, the parameter's name, or null
 * @param pointer              for an invalid request, the JSON pointer of the fault in the body,
 *                             the empty string for the body as a whole, or null
 * @param keyword              for an invalid request, the constraint violated, as the contract
 *                             spells it; null otherwise
 * @param request              the complete request
 * @param expectedStatus       the status the contract declares for it
 * @param expectedContentTypes every content type that response is declared with; empty when it
 *                             has no content, and only the status is expected
 * @param responseBodyClass    the simple name of the generated class for that response's body,
 *                             in this package, or null when it has none
 * @param operationId          the {@code operationId} of the case's operation, or null when the
 *                             contract gives it none
 * @param declaredQuery        the name of every query parameter the operation declares, whether
 *                             or not the request carries it, in declaration order
 * @param declaredHeaders      the name of every header parameter the operation declares, whether
 *                             or not the request carries it, in declaration order; without
 *                             {@code Accept}, {@code Content-Type} and {@code Authorization},
 *                             which OpenAPI ignores as parameters
 */
@com.arc_e_tect.sedr.utils.jacoco.marker.ExcludeFromJacocoGeneratedCodeCoverage(justification = "Generated by API-Only TranscriberJ")
public record ContractCase(String id, CaseKind kind, boolean requiresState, String variant, String description,
                           String in, String name, String pointer, String keyword, ContractRequest request,
                           int expectedStatus, java.util.List<String> expectedContentTypes, String responseBodyClass,
                           String operationId, java.util.List<String> declaredQuery,
                           java.util.List<String> declaredHeaders) {
}
